 `approved_for_canary`; production activation, canary promotion and release stay
 false until later signed observation evidence exists.
 
+
+## Manual qualification and cache trust scope
+
+Manual dispatch validates only the workflow's own `refs/heads/main` commit,
+selected by GitHub's immutable event SHA. It no longer accepts a PR number or
+fetches a different candidate for execution. Feature-branch or tag dispatches
+fail before checkout. Use the PR-triggered run or rerun that original run to
+qualify an unchanged PR head and synthetic merge in the PR event's scope. If
+the PR head/base advances, use its new PR-triggered run; old reruns fail the
+existing exact-parent/tree checks rather than relabeling a new merge. A manual main
+run does not substitute for either required PR lane.
+
+PR-source/controller checkouts are enabled only for `pull_request`. Main-source
+and main-controller checkouts use `github.sha`; the controller is checked
+against the source lane's exact identity before executing its scripts. Synthetic
+merge remains PR-only with exact parent/tree checks.
+
+This changes source selection, not cache permissions or repository settings.
+Read-only contents permission and disabled checkout credential persistence remain
+unchanged. CodeQL must evaluate the actual final workflow before the existing
+cache-security review threads can be considered resolved. Source regressions
+and this explanation do not waive those findings or grant activation.
